   "en": "§ The mishna teaches: When purchasing «jugs» of wine «in the Sharon» region, he accepts upon himself that up to ten inferior-quality jugs may be present in each hundred jugs purchased. «It was taught» in a baraita: The buyer must accept ten inferior-quality jugs in one hundred only when even those ten «inferior-quality jugs» are «beautiful and sealed with pitch» to strengthen them."
